# .dockerignore — DENY BY DEFAULT.
#
# WHY deny-by-default and not a deny-list of known-bad paths:
# the build context is uploaded to the daemon and anything COPY'd lands in an
# IMMUTABLE image layer. `RUN rm secret` does not remove it — the earlier layer
# still holds the file, and `docker history` / `docker save` / any `docker pull`
# of the published tag recovers it. A deny-list fails the moment someone adds a
# new file (a second .env, a CSV export, a Takeout dump); an allow-list fails
# closed instead: a new secret is invisible to the build until someone
# deliberately un-ignores it.
#
# This directory currently holds .env, .env.bak, data/ (every weigh-in, sleep
# and lift record) and input/manual.csv (waist measurements). None of it may
# ever reach a layer — the published image is a public artifact.
#
# Syntax note: `*` excludes everything at the context root (and, because Docker
# matches the full relative path, everything under those roots too). `!` lines
# re-include. Last matching rule wins, so the allow-list must come after `*`.

*

# ── The application, and only the application ──────────────────────────
!coach_sync
!coach_sync/**

# ── Dependency manifest + lockfile (installed frozen in the builder) ───
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock

# ── Public, non-personal metadata worth having inside the image ────────
!README.md
!LICENSE

# ── Belt and braces ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are already covered by `*`. They are restated so that a future edit
# which loosens the allow-list (e.g. someone adds `!*.toml` or `!.` ) cannot
# silently re-admit them: these lines come last, so they win.
.env
.env.*
campaign.toml
data
data/**
input
input/**
Takeout
Takeout/**
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.venv
.git
.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
tests
scripts
deploy
.github
